# The ACPI fan's _FST method is broken in this machine's firmware: every read of
# fan1_input returns -EIO, and each attempt evaluates failing AML that the kernel
# logs as an ACPI Error. KDE's ksystemstats polls it at 2 Hz -> ~8000 kernel
# errors per boot, which buries the ring buffer and was a large part of why the
# 2026-09-11 silent freezes appeared to leave "no trace".
#
# The sensor is 100% non-functional (never returns a value), so nothing is lost
# by hiding it from unprivileged readers. There is no cleaner lever: the driver
# is CONFIG_ACPI_FAN=y (built in, not blacklistable), /sys/bus/acpi/drivers has
# no fan entry to unbind, and cooling_device0 is in no thermal zone's cooling
# policy because the EC drives the fan in firmware anyway.
#
# Revert: delete this file, then `udevadm control --reload && udevadm trigger`.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="hwmon", ATTR{name}=="acpi_fan", \
  RUN+="/usr/bin/chmod 0600 /sys%p/fan1_input"
